; CommonTree2 — one of 2 "common" tree picks for the Forest terrain tile. Source: Stylized
; Nature MegaKit (Standard/free), Quaternius, CC0 1.0 Universal — see
; project/attribution/sources/quaternius_stylized_nature_megakit.tres.
;
; Scale is a FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL (same reasoning as CommonTree1): raw mesh height
; 7.642996 units -> scaled to the same ~2.5-tile canopy-height target (scale 0.327), so
; both common trees read a consistent height next to each other. FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF.
;
; LOOK-PASS REWORK (2026-08-16): this scene was imported but never wired as a live
; model_scene (CommonTree1 was the sole entry) and so never got the slab/floor treatment
; CommonTree1 received on 2026-08-03 — an oversight surfaced now that D-42's model_scenes
; array lets Forest actually alternate between both trees per tile. Brought to parity with
; CommonTree1: same Slab BoxMesh (0.94x0.2x0.94, Color(0.16, 0.4, 0.22, 1)) and the same 3
; blotchy floor patches (moss-dark-green / leaf-litter-brown PlaneMesh, unlit color
; treatment — no tileable ground texture exists in the audited packs, see CommonTree1.tscn's
; header for the fuller reasoning) at the same relative transforms, for a consistent forest
; floor regardless of which tree a tile lands on. FLAG FOR HUMAN SIGN-OFF, same as
; CommonTree1.
;
; ALL GROUND MESHES NESTED UNDER ONE NODE NAMED "Slab" (2026-08-16, required, not
; cosmetic) — same OcclusionFader exemption fix as CommonTree1.tscn; see that scene's
; header for the full reasoning. The BoxMesh ground plane (renamed "Ground") and all 3
; floor patches are children of a wrapper Node3D literally named "Slab" at identity
; transform.
;
; SLAB WIDENED 0.94 -> 1.0 (2026-08-16, human-reported cross-tile seam gap) — same fix,
; same reasoning, same exact-1.0-match approach as CommonTree1.tscn; see that scene's
; header for the full explanation. X/Z only, Y (0.2) untouched.
;
; SHORTENED TO 2.2 TILE-UNITS (2026-09-08, human ruling: "make Common Tree 2 a little shorter so
; we get some simple variety"). Scale 0.327 -> 0.28785 against a raw mesh AABB height of
; 7.642996 (0.28785 x 7.642996 = 2.200), about 12% down from the 2.5 it shared with every other
; tree in the terrain.
;
; THIS DELIBERATELY BREAKS THE "HEIGHT IS A CONTROL VARIABLE" RULE the rest of the Forest
; scenes state, and the break is the point. Every variant sitting at exactly 2.5 meant the only
; difference between neighbouring tiles was silhouette and foliage; one shorter tree gives a
; forest an uneven canopy line for free, with no new asset. CommonTree1 and CommonTree3 are
; UNCHANGED at 2.5 — the rule still holds for them, and for any variant added later. If a second
; variant is ever shortened, revisit this comment rather than quietly making 2.2 the new default.
;
; 2.2 IS NOT AN ARBITRARY NUMBER: it is the height DeadTree.tscn used for exactly this purpose
; ("deliberately shorter than the living-canopy trees") before the 2026-09-08 cull unwired it,
; so the terrain has one short tier rather than two competing ones.
;
; STILL A FIRST-PASS PROPOSAL in the sense every scale here is — no GDD number exists for tree
; height — but the RATIO is now a human ruling, not tech-art's guess.
;
; OCCLUSIONFADER REMOVED 2026-09-08 — ANY MENTION OF IT BELOW IS HISTORY. The per-resident
; transparency fade (D-41 §4) flickered in play and was cut outright; the script, its scene node
; and its two suites are gone. The "Slab" node stays, because every terrain scene is built
; around it and removing it would restructure all 33 for no gain — but NO CODE LOOKS THAT NAME
; UP ANY MORE. It is a grouping convention now, with no behaviour attached, so nothing breaks if
; a new scene groups differently and nothing is gained by "restoring" the exemption.
[gd_scene load_steps=8 format=3]

